## 6. Functional requirements

- FR-1: Users can list, create, view, edit, and delete records of every entity.
- FR-2: Foreign-key relations are enforced; orphan rows are rejected.
- FR-3: Every record has `id`, `created_at`, `updated_at` system columns.
- FR-4: All data for this app lives in the `{{ schema_name }}` Postgres schema.
{%- if bp.ai_enabled %}
- FR-5: An AI endpoint (`/api/ai`) is available to augment records or answer
  natural-language questions over the data.
{%- endif %}

## 7. Non-functional requirements

- NFR-1: The generated app must start with `npm run dev` or `docker run` without
  additional manual steps beyond configuring `DATABASE_URL`.
- NFR-2: Typecheck (`tsc --noEmit`) must pass for all generated code.
- NFR-3: Deterministic generation — regenerating from the same Blueprint must
  produce byte-identical files.

## 8. Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Every entity listed in section 5 has a working `/` list page and a
      `/<entity>/new` create form.
- [ ] Creating a child record with an invalid FK fails with a readable error.
- [ ] Deleting a parent record behaves per the generated SQL constraint.
- [ ] The app's schema exists in Postgres and contains one table per entity.
